# Frontend UX

- Evidence-first on company dossiers; sticky section nav for long pages.
- Universe table is the Screener hero job — no demo charts, no "demo tape", no scaffold markets on public pages.
- Show score **level + confidence tier + "as of"** always; show Δ (MoM/QoQ/YoY) **only** when the series is `citeable_pit` — otherwise `—`. Never a synthetic delta.
- Sorting: unscored / `—` rows sort **last** in both directions (`HomePage.tsx` sort comparator).
- Public dossier anatomy (guest/retail): header (score, tier, as-of, one-sentence record) → delivery record → evidence table → revision trail → how-calculated → methodology/changelog links. Everything else (extract, review queue, ledger PDF, analytics, wordmap, vernacular) is Workbench-only. Spec: skill `citealpha-expert-ux`.
- Metric names via `metricDisplayName()`; never raw ids in UI.
- Desk/Research: sync tabs via `?tab=`; sticky company picker where multi-tab.
- API only through `lib/api.ts`. Prefer `Toast` / `Skeleton` over bare muted status.
- Mobile: usable nav (toggle); desktop-first dense tables OK with horizontal scroll.
- Visual: Source Serif + IBM Plex; paper/ink palette; no purple glow / emoji chrome.
- Full prompt: `docs/prompts/PROFESSIONAL_SITE_PROMPT.md` · kb `docs/kb/06-frontend-ux.md`.
